{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR RULED: plumbing fix IN SCOPE for epic 061c; the 172e gap IN SCOPE; I may file tickets under the epic for in-scope work; the epic's mandate is to ship WITHOUT BUGS, so ASK before declaring any bug out of scope. Acted on all three.\n\n**FILED b690-f232-5bae-4b8b (antifungal-pine-swan)** — bug, parented to epic 061c, 5 file_impact entries set BEFORE review (so the attestation is scoped, per the 9227/eb58 lesson), linked as BLOCKING 3768. **Plan PASSED FIRST ROUND: 0 blocking, 1 advisory** — signed at 44d9250ea, CLAIMED. That first-round pass is worth noting against d23e's NINE rounds and 3768's four: the plan led with MEASURED evidence, explicitly ELIMINATED the competing hypotheses, stated what must NOT change, made the missing-test post-mortem the centrepiece, and gave every deliverable a criterion that can prove it.\n\nDIAGNOSIS IS AIRTIGHT ON BEHAVIOUR, OPEN ON MECHANISM — and I stopped rather than guess. Both plumbing halves look CORRECT in isolation: `runs.py:144-156` RunnerAgentStep resolves `resolve_model(cfg, step=ctx.step.get('model'), ...)` and code-review DOES pass `config=cfg`; `code_review/batch_runner.py:60-61,83-84` resolves `model_ladder[0]` and sets `step['model']`. The doc is untransformed (`_gate_doc(\"code-review\", ...)`). So source reading has NOT located the drop.\nAND THE LIVE LOG CANNOT LOCATE IT EITHER: `usage_log.record(op=...)` records the PROMPT NAME, not the step id, and `code-review-base` is the prompt for BOTH the `base` step AND the batch finder — so the nine ops cannot be attributed to steps. Attributing them by name would be exactly the inference error that has already produced three false starts this session.\n=> the recording-runner test in b690 is the DIAGNOSTIC, not merely the regression guard: it observes (step_id -> model handed to the runner), the one fact neither instrument yields. Write it, confirm RED, let it name the seam, fix that.\n\n172e: NOT reopened. Its evidence gap is covered by a b690 criterion that re-validates `verify`'s `model: standard` under the same test, so the behaviour gets pinned without churning a closed ticket. Flagged to the operator rather than decided silently.\n\nSTATE: 11 closed. Gerrit 1164 (d23e) + 1169 (3768) both +1/+1 submittable, NOTHING submitted. 3768 claimed/in_progress — YAML correct, blocked by b690 for its live-evidence criterion. b690 claimed and ready to implement. 0d76/eb6e/8625 blocked; 5e75 ready."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785608833345745001,"uuid":"c6f9b7c7-82f3-4151-b339-6dbdefcc875c"}